{"id": "f81f1b20-5225-4490-be6c-6527907ec72e", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll find the failed Nova Micro training job in this account and read its failure details and training logs. Then I'll tell you what went wrong and how to fix it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_383oB0zRy5uUg8EIeWbcej", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "sagemaker-nova-failure-check", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Find the failed SageMaker training job for a Nova Micro SFT + LoRA fine-tuning run and determine, from the recorded evidence, why it failed and how to fix it.",
  "context": "The user says their Nova Micro SFT+LoRA fine-tuning job on SageMaker failed and they don't know why. They want the cause and fix explained in chat. Use only read-only operations. Distinguish clearly between what the job record or logs explicitly state and anything you infer.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 012345678901_1", "region us-east-1 first; if nothing is found, check other regions where SageMaker is used", "SageMaker training jobs (also check SageMaker HyperPod / Nova customization recipes / model customization jobs if no standard training job matches)", "CloudWatch log group /aws/sagemaker/TrainingJobs"],
  "timeframe": "Most recent failures, roughly the last 14 days (current time 2026-11-24T18:52:08Z)",
  "criteria": "1) List training jobs with status Failed (newest first) and pick the one(s) that look like Nova Micro SFT/LoRA (job name, hyperparameters, recipe, image, instance type, model/ARN refs). If several candidates exist, report all briefly. 2) For the best match, call DescribeTrainingJob and report: job name, ARN, creation/end times, FailureReason, SecondaryStatus and StatusTransitions, instance type/count, algorithm/image, key hyperparameters/recipe settings, input data config (S3 URIs, content type), output config, role. 3) Read the job's CloudWatch logs (last ~200 lines before failure plus any ERROR/Exception/Traceback lines) and quote the exact error messages. 4) Check likely explicit causes only against evidence: S3 data format/schema errors (e.g., Nova SFT expects JSONL in Bedrock conversation format), missing/inaccessible S3 objects or IAM permission errors, KMS, instance type/quota (ResourceLimitExceeded), unsupported hyperparameter values (LoRA settings, global batch size, max length, epochs/learning rate), unsupported region/instance type, OOM, image/recipe mismatch. Consult AWS docs via verify_aws_claim for the Nova Micro SFT/LoRA requirements (supported instance types, data format, hyperparameter ranges) to propose a concrete fix. 5) Return: the exact failure reason from the record, supporting log lines, and a concise recommended fix with specifics. If the record/logs contain no cause, state explicitly that no cause is recorded rather than guessing, and list the concrete next checks. Say if you could not read any piece of the record."
}", "preloaded_skills": ["searching-logs", "verifying-with-docs"]}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Find failed Nova Micro SageMaker training job and analyze failure"}], "created_at": null}

